_type":"markdown","id":"b2744612","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006235,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:48:02.119735+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:48:02.1135+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Actual sample versus the full original dataset\n","\n","Keep up to `MAX_PER_CLASS = 300_000` randomly selected rows per `Attack`; retain every row from classes smaller than the cap. The cells compare this actual sample with the full original data before encoding, cleaning, splitting, or fitted transformations. No second reference sample or 50,000-row diagnostic cap is used.\n","\n","The class table measures the deliberate change in class proportions. Numerical features are compared within each Attack using KS distance: 0 means matching empirical CDFs; 0.02 means a maximum CDF gap of 2 percentage points. Nominal fields use total variation distance between category frequencies (0 means matching frequencies). Missing and infinite rates are reported separately. Both distances range from 0 to 1; no universal pass/fail cutoff is imposed. Read the complete tables in `numeric_distribution_report` and `categorical_distribution_report`.\n","\n","These are descriptive comparisons. KS p-values are not reported because the sample is a subset of the original, many features are discrete, and a small p-value would not establish a practically important difference. Marginal agreement does not prove matching correlations, rare subgroups, or tails. Keeping every minority row gives matching raw distributions for that class; it does not add new independent observations.\n","\n","`CHECK_SAMPLE_DISTRIBUTION = False` skips the feature comparisons while retaining the class table and releasing the original. Full-data comparisons may take time; they process one column at a time and print each class. Rerun **Load and inspect** before repeating sampling.\n","\n","Sampling remains before the split in this workflow: validation/test therefore reflect the capped class mix. For evaluation at the original class proportions, split the original data first and cap training only. Preprocessing is still fitted after splitting."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"f66ff557","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-10T11:48:02.134268Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-10T11:48:02.13377Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-10T11:48:07.410539Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-10T11:48:07.409662Z"},"papermill":{"duration":5.286438,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:48:07.412567+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:48:02.126129+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Original: 11,503,556 rows | Actual sample: 939,236 rows\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Original rows</th>\n","      <th>Sample rows</th>\n","      <th>Original (%)</th>\n","      <th>Sample (%)</th>\n","      <th>Difference (percentage points)</th>\n","      <th>Rows retained (%)</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Attack</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Benign</th>\n","      <td>38435</td>\n","      <td>38435</td>\n","      <td>0.3341</td>\n","      <td>4.0922</td>\n","      <td>3.7580</td>\n","      <td>100.0000</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>DDoS</th>\n","      <td>4786502</td>\n","      <td>300000</td>\n","      <td>41.6089</td>\n","      <td>31.9409</td>\n","      <td>-9.6680</td>\n","      <td>6