        (finite > np.finfo(np.float32).max) |\n","            (finite < -np.finfo(np.float32).max)\n","        ).sum(),\n","        'outside_float64': (\n","            (finite > np.finfo(np.float64).max) |\n","            (finite < -np.finfo(np.float64).max)\n","        ).sum(),\n","    })\n","\n","outlier_report = pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index('feature')\n","with pd.option_context('display.max_rows', None):\n","    display(outlier_report)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d9a5c762","metadata":{"id":"578df466","papermill":{"duration":0.009,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:49:54.695711+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:49:54.686711+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 8. Fit preprocessing on training data only\n","\n","This CIC notebook previously had no PCA. `PCA_COMPONENTS = None` preserves its existing numeric outputs. To enable PCA over **all scaled numeric measurement columns**, choose an integer component count (no larger than the number of numeric features and fitting rows). Protocol one-hot columns stay outside PCA.\n","\n","Set `PCA_FIT_ROWS = IMPUTER_FIT_ROWS` for sampled PCA, `None` for full-training PCA, or another positive cap. Pass these into `make_preprocessor(..., pca_fit_rows=PCA_FIT_ROWS, n_components=PCA_COMPONENTS)`. PCA changes the numeric output columns and requires retraining downstream models.\n","\n","The CIC imputer and numeric scaler retain their existing sampled fitting behavior, now controlled by `IMPUTER_FIT_ROWS`. One-hot vocabularies include all observed training categories. Learned branches are frozen and assembled with one preview row, avoiding a combined full-training feature matrix. All fitting uses training rows only; transforms/writes remain batched. Full-train PCA mode can still require substantial RAM. Requires scikit-learn >= 1.6.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":28,"id":"156391a9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-10T11:49:54.715904Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-10T11:49:54.715513Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.181469Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.180174Z"},"id":"8cac2998","papermill":{"duration":536.478874,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.183747+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:49:54.704873+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Fitting CIC imputer/scaler on 500,000 training rows...\n","[IterativeImputer] Completing matrix with shape (500000, 76)\n","[IterativeImputer] Change: 0.0, scaled tolerance: 917530.88 \n","[IterativeImputer] Early stopping criterion reached.\n","[Pipeline] .. (step 1 of 2) Processing iterativeimputer, total= 8.9min\n","[Pipeline]  (step 2 of 2) Processing quantiletransformer, total=   0.1s\n","CIC PCA disabled (n_components=None).\n","[IterativeImputer] Completing matrix with shape (1, 76)\n","[ColumnTransformer] ....... (1 of 2) Processing numbers, total=   0.0s\n","[ColumnTransformer] .... (2 of 2) Processing categories, total=   0.0s\n","CIC preprocessor ready: 79 features.\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.experimental import enable_iterative_imputer\n","from sklearn.impute import IterativeImputer\n","\n","def category_fit_frame(data, columns):\n","    \"\"\"Fit independent category vocabularies without expanding millions of rows.\"\"\"\n","    values = {c: pd.Series(data[c]).drop_duplicates().to_numpy() for c in columns}\n","    longest = max(map(len, values.values()))\n","    # Repeat real values to align column lengths; do not invent missing categories.\n","    return pd.DataFrame({c: np.resize(v, longest) for c, v in values.items()})\n","\n","\n","def fit_pca(data, columns, preprocessing, n_components=1, fit_rows=None,\n","            random_state=42, verbose=True):\n","    \"\"\"fit_rows=None uses all training rows; an integer caps PCA fitting rows.\"\"\"\n","    if fit_rows is not None and fit_rows < 1:\n","        raise ValueError('fit_rows must be None or a positive row count.')\n","    if fit_rows is None or fit_rows >= len(data):\n","        fit_data = data[columns]\n","    else:\n","        fit_data = data.sample(n=fit_rows, random_state=random_state)[columns]\n","    if verbose:\n","        print(f'PCA fit: {len(fit_data):,}/{len(data):,} training rows; '\n","              f'{len(columns)} inputs -> {n_components} component(s).', flush=True)\n","    model = make_pipeline(\n","        *[step for _, step in preprocessing.steps],\n","        PCA(n_components=n_components, svd_solver='full'),\n","        verbose=verbose,\n","    )\n","    model.fit(fit_data)\n","    model.fit_rows_ = len(fit_data)\n","    if verbose:\n","        retained = model.steps[-1][1].explained_variance_ratio_.sum()\n","        print(f'PCA fitted; retained variance: {retained:.2%}.', flush=True)\n","    return model\n","\n","\n","def make_preprocessor(train, numeric_cols, one_hot, scaler=None,\n","                      imputer_fit_rows=500_000, pca_fit_rows=None,\n","                      n_components=None, random_state=42, verbose=True):\n","    \"\"\"Optional PCA over scaled numeric measurements; categories remain separate.\"\"\"\n","    sample = train.sample(\n","        n=min(imputer_fit_rows, len(train)), random_state=random_state,\n","    )[numeric_cols]\n","    imputer = IterativeImputer(max_iter=5, random_state=random_state, verbose=int(verbose))\n","    numeric_scaler = StandardScaler() if scaler is None else clone(scaler)\n","    numbers = make_pipeline(imputer, numeric_scaler, verbose=verbose)\n","    if verbose:\n","        print(f'Fitting CIC imputer/scaler on {len(sample):,} training rows...', flush=True)\n","    numbers.fit(sample)\n","    imputer_rows = len(sample)\n","    del sample\n","\n","    # Preserve the original CIC numeric fit cap. PCA has its own independent cap.\n","    if n_components is not None:\n","        numbers_branch = fit_pca(\n","            train, numeric_cols, preprocessing=make_pipeline(FrozenEstimator(numbers)),\n","            n_components=n_components, fit_rows=pca_fit_rows,\n","            random_state=random_state, verbose=verbose,\n","        )\n","    else:\n","        numbers_branch = numbers\n","        if verbose:\n","            print('CIC PCA disabled (n_components=None).', flush=True)\n","    categories = OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore').fit(\n","        category_fit_frame(train, one_hot)\n","    )\n","    result = ColumnTransformer([\n","        ('numbers', FrozenEstimator(numbers_branch), numeric_cols),\n","        ('categories', FrozenEstimator(categories), one_hot),\n","    ], verbose=verbose)\n","    result.fit(train.iloc[:1])\n","    result.imputer_ = imputer\n","    result.numeric_scaler_ = numeric_scaler\n","    result.imputer_fit_rows_ = imputer_rows\n","    result.pca_ = numbers_branch.steps[-1][1] if n_components is not None else None\n","    if verbose:\n","        print(f'CIC preprocessor ready: {len(result.get_feature_names_out()):,} features.', flush=True)\n","    return result\n","\n","\n","preprocessor = make_preprocessor(\n","    train, numeric_cols, col_to_one_hot,\n","    scaler=NUMERIC_SCALER, imputer_fit_rows=IMPUTER_FIT_ROWS,\n","    pca_fit_rows=PCA_FIT_ROWS, n_components=PCA_COMPONENTS,\n","    random_state=SEED, verbose=PREPROCESSING_VERBOSE,\n",")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c3cf7236","metadata":{"id":"03010a74","papermill":{"duration":0.01013,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.203329+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.193199+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Save each split below in batches, then release its original frame. To repeat saving or run the optional raw-data benchmarks afterward, rerun the loading/splitting cells first."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"95af4940","metadata":{"id":"ffe9484b","papermill":{"duration":0.009748,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.222436+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:58:51.212688+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 9. Transform, save