IoT/preprocessing/20261110_all_attacks_IterativeImputer\n"]}],"source":["from datetime import datetime\n","import gc\n","import joblib\n","import sklearn\n","import pyarrow as pa\n","import pyarrow.parquet as pq\n","from scipy.sparse import issparse\n","\n","PROJECT = Path(OUTPATH)\n","fitted_imputer = preprocessor.imputer_\n","fitted_numeric_scaler = preprocessor.numeric_scaler_\n","fitted_pca = preprocessor.pca_\n","attack_tag = f\"holdout_{HELD_OUT_ATTACK}\" if HOLD_OUT_ATTACK else \"all_attacks\"\n","RUN_NAME = f\"{datetime.now():%Y%m%d}_{attack_tag}_{type(fitted_imputer).__name__}\"\n","OUTPUT_DIR = PROJECT / 'outputs' / DATASET / 'preprocessing' / RUN_NAME\n","OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","BATCH_SIZE = 10000  # Reduce this if a transformed batch still uses too much RAM.\n","joblib.dump(preprocessor, OUTPUT_DIR / 'preprocessor.joblib', compress=0)\n","\n","# Move frames into the queue; remove the other references so they can be freed.\n","splits = {'train': train, 'val': val, 'test': test}\n","if HOLD_OUT_ATTACK:\n","    splits['zero_day'] = zero_day\n","del train, val, test, zero_day\n","counts = []\n","for name in list(splits):\n","    rows = splits.pop(name)\n","    with pq.ParquetWriter(OUTPUT_DIR / f'{name}.parquet', schema, compression='zstd') as writer:\n","        for start in range(0, len(rows), BATCH_SIZE):\n","            batch = rows.iloc[start:start + BATCH_SIZE]\n","            X = preprocessor.transform(batch[feature_cols])\n","            # # Reduce batch memory before densifying sparse output.\n","            # # float32 rounding is intentional for compact model inputs.\n","            # X = X.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n","            # Densify this small batch only; never the complete split.\n","            if issparse(X):\n","                X = X.toarray()\n","            prepared = pd.DataFrame(X, columns=feature_names)\n","            prepared['Label'] = batch['Label'].to_numpy()\n","            prepared['Attack'] = batch['Attack'].to_numpy()\n","            table = pa.Table.from_pandas(prepared, schema=schema, preserve_index=False)\n","            writer.write_table(table)\n","            del batch, X, prepared, table\n","    counts.append(f'- {name}: {len(rows):,} rows')\n","    print('Saved and released:', name, len(rows), 'rows')\n","    del rows\n","    gc.collect()  # Frees Python references; the allocator may retain some reserved RAM.\n","\n","holdout_note = f\"Reserve `{HELD_OUT_ATTACK}` as zero-day data\" if HOLD_OUT_ATTACK else \"Use all attack classes; no separate zero-day set\"\n","saved_files = '`train.parquet`, `val.parquet`, `test.parquet`' + (', `zero_day.parquet`' if HOLD_OUT_ATTACK else '')\n","readme = f\"\"\"# {DATASET} preprocessing — {RUN_NAME}\n","\n","Source: `{DATA_DIR / FILES[DATASET]}`\n","Holdout enabled: `{HOLD_OUT_ATTACK}`. Held-out attack: `{HELD_OUT_ATTACK if HOLD_OUT_ATTACK else \"None (all attacks included)\"}`. Seed: `{SEED}`. scikit-learn: `{sklearn.__version__}`.\n","\n","## Sampling and comparison\n","Before cleaning and splitting, retain up to {MAX_PER_CLASS:,} random rows per Attack class and all rows from smaller classes. Compare the actual sample to the full original using class proportions, within-class numerical KS distance, and categorical total variation. Diagnostics do not use another reference sample. Validation/test reflect the capped class mix.\n","\n","## Steps followed\n","1. Inspect data and attack counts; strip column/attack-name whitespace.\n","2. Remove dataset identifiers, IP addresses, and generated index columns.\n","3. Treat PROTOCOL, L7_PROTO, DNS_QUERY_TYPE, and FTP_COMMAND_RET_CODE as categories, fill missing categories with 'missing', and replace numeric infinities with NaN.\n","4. Remove rows missing targets and exact duplicate rows.\n","5. {holdout_note}; split eligible traffic 70/15/15, stratified by Attack. With holdout disabled, attack classes are eligible for every split; rare classes are not guaranteed to occur in each split.\n","6. Fit `{fitted_imputer!r}` and `{fitted_numeric_scaler!r}` on {preprocessor.imputer_fit_rows_:,} sampled training rows (cap {IMPUTER_FIT_ROWS:,}). One-hot vocabularies include all observed training categories. Optional numeric PCA: {PCA_COMPONENTS!r} components; requested PCA row cap: {PCA_FIT_ROWS!r}; actual PCA fit rows: {fitted_pca.n_samples_ if fitted_pca is not None else 'disabled'}. PCA variance retained: {fitted_pca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum() if fitted_pca is not None else 'disabled'}. All fitting uses training data only; branches are frozen and assembled with one preview row.\n","7. Transform each split in batches of at most {BATCH_SIZE:,} rows and write directly to Parquet with Zstandard compression.\n","8. Release each batch and completed split before continuing.\n","\n","## Saved files\n","{saved_files} contain TRANSFORMED numeric feature columns plus `Label` and `Attack`.\n","Features are already imputed, encoded, and scaled: do not transform them again.\n","`preprocessor.joblib` is for new RAW data only. Feature order is `preprocessor.get_feature_names_out()`.\n","Storage types: scaled numerical features or optional numeric PCA outputs use float32; one-hot features use uint8. The configured SECOND_BYTES numeric outputs retain float64 when present. Protocol one-hot outputs remain outside PCA.\n","Label and Attack retain their original Arrow types. The same schema is used for every batch and split.\n","Float32 reduces precision compared with float64.\n","These files differ from older exports of cleaned, untransformed features.\n","\n","{chr(10).join(counts)}\n","\n","## Read prepared batches\n","```python\n","import pyarrow.parquet as pq\n","for record_batch in pq.ParquetFile('train.parquet').iter_batches(batch_size=10000):\n","    batch = record_batch.to_pandas()\n","    X = batch.drop(columns=['Label', 'Attack'])\n","    y = batch['Label']\n","    # Consume this batch directly; do not apply preprocessor.transform(X).\n","```\n","\n","Initial loading/splitting and imputer fitting still require RAM. Full-train PCA can require substantial RAM; set PCA_FIT_ROWS to a smaller cap. To reload preprocessor.joblib, use scikit-learn >= 1.6; no custom transformer class is required. Saving releases the original split frames; rerun loading/splitting before using raw-data benchmarks or repeating the save step.\n","Row splits and exact deduplication do not guarantee session isolation or isolation of identical predictors with conflicting labels.\n","\"\"\"\n","(OUTPUT_DIR / 'README.md').write_text(readme, encoding='utf-8')\n","print('Prepared datasets saved to:', OUTPUT_DIR)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"8dd1a802","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.012147,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.895219+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.883072+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"dd557862","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.012915,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.920332+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.907417+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 7. Class Imbalance"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3c73e906","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.01226,"end_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.944782+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.932522+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Load the processed `train.parquet`, resample its `Attack` classes with ADASYN, then clean the original majority Attack class with Tomek Links. Exclude both targets from features. Restore binary `Label` from the original Attack-to-Label mapping when saving. Validation and test are not resampled here. Synthetic one-hot coordinates can be fractional and remain floating point."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":31,"id":"bfaa1fea","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.970972Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-10T11:59:14.970637Z","iop