:59:20.494559+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["ADASYN uses an explicit dictionary of desired class counts. Classes already within `ADASYN_BALANCE_TOLERANCE = 0.01` (1%) of the largest class are left unchanged. This avoids requesting a negligible top-up such as 29 samples across 209,971 Reconnaissance rows, where every per-row allocation can round to zero.\n","\n","The 1% tolerance is an explicit policy, not a requirement of ADASYN. Smaller classes target the largest count; the generated counts remain approximate. There is no silent fallback to another sampler. Independent ADASYN failures, such as unsuitable neighborhoods, remain visible."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":33,"id":"143c1f65","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-10T11:59:20.534007Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-10T11:59:20.533403Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-10T12:00:50.629197Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-10T12:00:50.62815Z"},"papermill":{"duration":90.113054,"end_time":"2026-11-10T12:00:50.632405+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-10T11:59:20.519351+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["ADASYN desired class counts: {'Benign': 210000, 'Theft': 210000}\n","After ADASYN (Attack):\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Before</th>\n","      <th>After ADASYN</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Attack</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Benign</th>\n","      <td>26848</td>\n","      <td>209520</